WEBVTT

00:22.480 --> 00:24.733
Where did you disappear to?

00:25.900 --> 00:29.654
No one could ever take your place.

00:30.447 --> 00:35.035
Everyone here tried to be like you.

00:38.079 --> 00:41.124
But no one can replace you.

00:44.961 --> 00:46.379
PAPER PLANE
WITH FOLDING GUIDE

01:04.064 --> 01:06.816
Please come back soon.

01:15.742 --> 01:18.119
I can't find it at all.

01:18.787 --> 01:25.752
But the info about the Cross-Eyes' hideout
here in Berith was supposed to be solid.

01:26.252 --> 01:30.173
LET'S USE OUR RESOURCES WITH CARE
BERITH NEWS

01:32.884 --> 01:37.097
How many years has it been
since I died, anyway?

01:39.849 --> 01:41.142
Welcome.

01:44.646 --> 01:46.106
I beg you.

01:46.189 --> 01:51.361
I was planning to just pay with coupons,
so I didn't bring my wallet.

01:51.861 --> 01:53.863
I guess it can't be helped.

01:53.947 --> 01:56.407
I'll give you a little discount today.

01:56.491 --> 01:57.700
Thank you.

02:02.997 --> 02:05.500
- All right, I'll come by again.
- Thank you.

02:06.334 --> 02:07.418
Welcome.

02:08.503 --> 02:10.421
That will be 130 nicks.

02:11.673 --> 02:12.966
Thank you!

02:15.218 --> 02:16.594
- What's up?
- What?

02:19.222 --> 02:20.682
What's your deal?

02:20.765 --> 02:23.393
You're Risu, aren't you?

02:25.395 --> 02:27.689
It's not like we've met before.

03:57.028 --> 03:58.947
THE BEGINNING

04:08.539 --> 04:10.708
This is our hideout.

04:17.340 --> 04:21.594
I didn't think
it would be such a normal house.

04:21.678 --> 04:25.556
I thought it would be
more secret society-like.

04:28.101 --> 04:29.811
I bought some rice.

04:32.063 --> 04:33.314
Hey, guys.

04:33.398 --> 04:34.941
Risu is here.

04:47.912 --> 04:50.581
Isn't it a little bit too dark here?

04:50.665 --> 04:52.667
Why don't you turn on the lights?

04:53.710 --> 04:56.587
It's our rule. No lights during the day.

04:57.171 --> 04:59.090
Hey, pour him some tea.

04:59.173 --> 05:02.468
We can still use yesterday's tea bag.

05:02.552 --> 05:04.012
Here you go.

05:06.139 --> 05:08.558
I heard you were dead.

05:09.183 --> 05:11.728
I'm looking for the guy who killed me!

05:11.811 --> 05:16.149
The guy who killed you?
What do you mean? You're alive.

05:16.232 --> 05:17.734
I was resurrected!

05:17.817 --> 05:19.986
Through the Magic of En's pet!

05:20.069 --> 05:22.238
- Chawantake?
- You mean Kikurage?

05:25.325 --> 05:29.203
The one who killed me
was a Cross-Eyes man.

05:29.287 --> 05:30.747
I witnessed it myself.

05:30.830 --> 05:34.000
Where is he? Where's the boss?
Let me see him now!

05:34.584 --> 05:35.752
Or else...

05:36.753 --> 05:38.838
Well, why don't you calm down?

05:41.716 --> 05:45.053
There's nothing we know about your death.

05:46.304 --> 05:47.930
Old newspapers, magazines.

05:48.014 --> 05:49.307
Do you hear that?

05:50.141 --> 05:55.813
Feel free to call out to me if there's
anything you don't need anymore.

05:56.481 --> 05:57.940
The newspaper collector!

05:58.024 --> 06:01.235
Five stacks of old news
equals three rolls of toilet paper.

06:02.153 --> 06:03.321
Go after him!

06:08.993 --> 06:13.206
That was a surprise.
That collector is so hard to track down.

06:13.289 --> 06:17.460
Who cares about old newspapers?!
Just turn on the lights already!

06:17.543 --> 06:20.463
No. We won't until the sun has set.

06:25.885 --> 06:28.721
Give me a break, guys.

06:29.514 --> 06:33.726
I think it's already dark enough outside.

06:34.769 --> 06:37.480
It's also starting to affect our work.

06:37.563 --> 06:39.732
- I think it's about time.
- Right.

06:44.946 --> 06:46.864
I'm Tetsujo. Nice to meet you.

06:46.948 --> 06:47.990
I'm Ton.

06:48.074 --> 06:48.991
Saji.

06:49.075 --> 06:50.493
I'm Ushishimada.

06:51.077 --> 06:52.578
My name is Dokuga.

06:53.079 --> 06:56.541
I've heard your names before.

06:56.624 --> 06:58.751
You're the guys closest to the boss.

06:58.835 --> 07:02.255
More importantly, Risu,
how long are you planning to stay?

07:03.423 --> 07:07.009
Sounds like me being here
might bring you some trouble.

07:07.593 --> 07:10.346
We don't have enough food
to feed you dinner.

07:10.430 --> 07:11.264
You heard him.

07:11.347 --> 07:13.057
Come on, boys. Time to eat.

07:13.141 --> 07:15.101
Who's in charge of cooking today?

07:16.978 --> 07:19.397
The boss is this way.

07:21.524 --> 07:23.693
Welcome.

07:23.776 --> 07:25.820
What are you doing, Ebisu?

07:25.903 --> 07:28.865
They're putting me to work.

07:28.948 --> 07:32.201
If you don't work, you don't eat.
That's the rule.

07:32.285 --> 07:37.206
I'm the seductive
man-eating mermaid, Erabisu.

07:37.290 --> 07:41.002
Man-eating? Is this a cannibal club?

07:41.085 --> 07:42.962
It's a figure of speech.

07:43.045 --> 07:45.214
Good, you're here.

07:46.174 --> 07:47.258
Give them alcohol.

07:47.341 --> 07:48.968
Yes, Big Boss!

07:49.051 --> 07:51.721
- You, bring them some women.
- Yes, sir!

07:51.804 --> 07:53.431
I don't need that!

07:55.850 --> 07:58.102
- Good evening.
- Hi.

07:58.186 --> 07:59.312
Hello there.

08:01.856 --> 08:03.816
Hello, both of you!

08:05.401 --> 08:07.945
What? Even Fujita is working here?

08:08.029 --> 08:11.532
I volunteered to take care
of Mr. En's daily needs.

08:11.616 --> 08:15.077
He follows me everywhere.
He's annoying as hell, honestly.

08:17.663 --> 08:21.584
Nikaido, I knew I couldn't trust you.

08:21.667 --> 08:24.587
I'll protect Mr. En no matter what.

08:24.670 --> 08:26.339
So annoying.

08:29.675 --> 08:31.093
Your martinis.

08:32.011 --> 08:33.387
Please enjoy.

08:34.180 --> 08:35.598
There's been some news.

08:36.182 --> 08:37.475
I finally found it.

08:38.267 --> 08:40.853
The place making the black powder.

08:40.937 --> 08:42.355
- What?
- For real?

08:42.438 --> 08:44.106
It's just a rumor, though.

08:44.190 --> 08:46.859
It seems there's a hideout in some forest.

08:46.943 --> 08:51.614
Saying it's in "some forest"
doesn't qualify as finding it, idiot!

08:52.949 --> 08:54.825
Was he there too?

08:55.576 --> 08:58.996
Maybe. That's what I suspect.

08:59.080 --> 09:01.874
You mean the leader of the Cross-Eyes?

09:01.958 --> 09:03.376
I saw it in the movie.

09:03.459 --> 09:06.379
En, you were
so wonderful in that! Seriously!

09:07.463 --> 09:08.422
I know, right?

09:08.506 --> 09:11.884
The scene where the family forms
gave me the chills!

09:11.968 --> 09:15.721
Doesn't Nikaido seem
to be acting more like Chota?

09:15.805 --> 09:17.974
Yeah, I think so too.

09:18.057 --> 09:21.227
The poor girl's got
her entire personality twisted up.

09:25.231 --> 09:28.985
I feel bad for Nikaido,
but at least we get to live.

09:29.068 --> 09:30.403
I'm so relieved.

09:30.486 --> 09:34.407
I'm also giving up on Nikaido.

09:34.949 --> 09:37.410
I'm not a good match with Sorcerers.

09:37.493 --> 09:41.414
I think Sorcerers and humans
can suit each other without a problem.

09:43.374 --> 09:48.296
Still, I would like to let Caiman know
about the current situation, at least.

09:58.973 --> 09:59.974
That's right.

10:00.057 --> 10:03.811
Since Caiman is immune to Magic,
he might be able to save Nikaido.

10:03.894 --> 10:08.107
But we don't know
where Caiman is right now.

10:08.858 --> 10:10.276
Let's send him a messenger.

10:13.654 --> 10:15.823
But who'd go?

10:17.283 --> 10:18.868
My wife.

10:20.411 --> 10:22.830
Thank you very much!

10:23.414 --> 10:26.125
Please come again!

10:27.752 --> 10:31.297
He's definitely still alive.
Don't you think so, Noi?

10:31.380 --> 10:32.965
I do.

10:33.049 --> 10:38.262
If we only knew his face,
there would be so many ways to find him.

10:39.055 --> 10:42.767
That bastard's face
was covered in Tenjin's blood.

10:42.850 --> 10:46.604
I couldn't even see the crosses
that should've been on his eyes.

10:47.938 --> 10:53.986
En's movie has a lot of crap,
but it's true that guy almost killed us.

11:00.868 --> 11:04.163
Shin, things are finally
getting interesting again.

11:04.246 --> 11:06.290
Next time I won't lose. I swear.

11:08.084 --> 11:10.252
You know what's good about you, Noi?

11:11.504 --> 11:15.174
No matter how dangerous the job,
you never weigh me down.

11:16.634 --> 11:18.260
You too, Shin.

11:21.013 --> 11:25.851
We left without a word to Shin.
He's probably furious right about now.

11:25.935 --> 11:28.938
I did leave a note, so it should be fine.

11:29.021 --> 11:31.148
Sorry it's tight, Jonson.

11:31.232 --> 11:32.441
Shocking!

11:36.946 --> 11:41.826
Will they be okay? If someone finds out
they're humans, they'll probably get sold.

11:41.909 --> 11:44.829
They said they'll come back by morning.
Let them be.

11:49.959 --> 11:51.168
Thanks.

11:51.252 --> 11:54.213
Shin, I'll go bring them back.

11:54.296 --> 11:56.882
Don't worry.
Why would you need to do that?

11:56.966 --> 12:00.219
I've been bored lately,
so I have too much spare energy.

12:00.845 --> 12:01.846
Hey, wait.

12:01.929 --> 12:03.848
All right, I'm off.

12:04.432 --> 12:05.433
Hey.

12:07.059 --> 12:09.103
Can't be helped, I guess.

12:12.106 --> 12:15.276
Doc, how long's it been
since you last saw your wife?

12:15.359 --> 12:19.363
- Let me think. About 25 years, maybe?
- What?!

12:19.447 --> 12:21.532
Are you sure she didn't dump you?

12:21.615 --> 12:24.493
Based on her age,
there's a chance she's dead.

12:24.577 --> 12:26.370
- Come on!
- What's that?

12:26.954 --> 12:28.748
There's a house.

12:33.586 --> 12:35.421
What's wrong, Jonson?

12:35.504 --> 12:37.631
He got stuck and can't get out.

12:38.966 --> 12:41.886
We'll be back in a moment,
so please wait here.

12:45.389 --> 12:46.766
So scary.

12:49.852 --> 12:51.395
Maybe she's not home?

12:51.896 --> 12:54.273
- It's open.
- Hey, wait!

13:00.488 --> 13:03.407
HORROR! BLOODY MANSION SLAUGHTER DANCE

13:04.241 --> 13:06.035
This can't be the place!

13:06.118 --> 13:10.289
We can't say that for sure.
Doc's house looked quite similar to this.

13:10.372 --> 13:11.415
What the hell!

13:13.000 --> 13:14.168
What?

13:14.752 --> 13:16.212
This is weird.

13:16.295 --> 13:18.422
Everything in here is almost as if...

13:19.006 --> 13:21.425
It seems there's another room in the back.

13:25.554 --> 13:26.514
What?

13:40.569 --> 13:43.197
Did you get lost, young ladies?

13:45.783 --> 13:50.454
No. They're the prey he sent us.

13:54.083 --> 13:55.960
It might be the wrong house.

13:56.043 --> 13:57.211
Jonson! Come here!

14:06.262 --> 14:07.930
What's that monster?

14:08.013 --> 14:11.433
Go, Jonson! Get rid of those guys!

14:16.063 --> 14:16.981
Knives don't work!

14:19.900 --> 14:22.570
- Let's escape while we can.
- Hold on to me!

14:23.612 --> 14:25.281
The entrance is...

14:25.364 --> 14:27.324
Damn bug, always messing things up!

14:27.408 --> 14:29.785
- This way!
- Jeez!

14:30.619 --> 14:33.163
Nishinoya, take care of those brats!

14:33.247 --> 14:34.540
All right!

14:39.670 --> 14:40.921
Hiratsuka!

14:53.851 --> 14:55.519
What should we do, Kento?

14:56.687 --> 14:58.731
I don't know if it will work, but...

14:58.814 --> 14:59.732
Take this!

15:06.697 --> 15:08.616
Crap, they're coming after us.

15:13.203 --> 15:16.582
- It's cold.
- You two wait here. I'll act as a decoy.

15:16.665 --> 15:17.583
Doc...

15:28.385 --> 15:29.637
Hey!

15:29.720 --> 15:31.263
Over here!

15:36.226 --> 15:37.519
A dead end.

15:41.941 --> 15:42.775
What?

15:43.609 --> 15:45.778
That's Haru and me.

15:49.365 --> 15:51.158
Found you!

15:51.742 --> 15:56.205
I'll cut you into pieces right now!

15:56.872 --> 16:01.794
Did you guys kill Haru
and steal this house from her?

16:17.601 --> 16:19.103
He's quite a tough one.

16:19.186 --> 16:22.147
Yeah, but not for much longer.

16:22.231 --> 16:24.400
See you in hell, you filthy--

16:26.860 --> 16:28.028
What the...

16:32.449 --> 16:37.746
Don't you bunch know the phrase
"tread on a worm and it will turn"?

16:37.830 --> 16:40.791
And this is my acquaintance's
acquaintance's insect.

16:40.874 --> 16:43.836
So if you're looking for a fight,
I'm right here.

16:43.919 --> 16:46.797
Go eat some sap or whatever it is you do.

16:47.881 --> 16:51.385
Huh? Now that I look at you,
aren't you Cross-Eyes?

16:51.468 --> 16:54.638
My worrying saved me the trouble
of having to hunt you down.

16:54.722 --> 16:59.268
This is Noi, En's cousin
and a healing-type Sorcerer.

16:59.351 --> 17:01.145
We got us a worthy prey.

17:02.229 --> 17:04.148
Come on, I'll rip you apart.

17:05.482 --> 17:07.651
Thank you for this, Boss.

17:11.697 --> 17:15.242
Well, well.
Looks like I ended up coming too.

17:16.785 --> 17:18.579
Little Bug? What's wrong?

17:18.662 --> 17:21.081
Shocking!

17:24.168 --> 17:27.087
This asshole was a woman?

17:27.171 --> 17:29.339
But you were amazing, Kento.

17:29.423 --> 17:32.092
To think you knocked Noi out in one hit.

17:32.176 --> 17:35.345
I just did what the boss taught me to do.

17:36.680 --> 17:39.683
I'll dismember her. Rip off her clothes.

17:40.184 --> 17:41.101
Got it.

17:47.316 --> 17:49.985
You guys seem to be having fun.

17:50.569 --> 17:51.737
Shin!

17:52.321 --> 17:53.322
Don't move!

17:54.656 --> 17:59.745
If I slightly twist this knife,
as if I were turning a tap,

17:59.828 --> 18:03.082
the Devil tumor inside her head
will become such a mess

18:03.165 --> 18:07.878
that not even Kikurage
would be able to resurrect her.

18:17.012 --> 18:18.972
Aren't you a fast learner?

18:19.473 --> 18:22.601
Take this! And this!

18:26.271 --> 18:27.106
And this!

18:28.357 --> 18:30.609
Noi, if it were you...

18:30.692 --> 18:34.029
Shin, fight without worrying about me.

18:34.113 --> 18:38.367
I'd rather die than let myself
get beaten without a fight.

18:38.450 --> 18:40.869
You'd probably say something like that.

18:41.411 --> 18:44.873
But you know what? I just...

19:16.572 --> 19:18.657
Yeah, it's no use.

19:20.242 --> 19:23.620
I'm so pissed off
that I can't take it anymore.

19:25.998 --> 19:27.666
Ouch.

19:27.749 --> 19:29.626
Somehow, I'm still alive.

19:29.710 --> 19:31.170
Found you!

19:33.714 --> 19:35.132
Prepare yourself!

19:38.594 --> 19:41.013
- Are you okay, Mr. Kasukabe?
- Shin!

19:41.096 --> 19:44.516
- You came to save us.
- It's dangerous, so stand back.

19:44.600 --> 19:46.351
But Shin, your injuries...

19:47.936 --> 19:50.105
My consciousness is fading away.

19:50.189 --> 19:53.275
No choice but to use Magic
and finish things quickly.

19:53.358 --> 19:54.484
It ran away.

19:54.568 --> 19:56.236
No, that's not it.

19:57.237 --> 20:00.407
The bastard knows
what kind of Magic I can do.

20:01.074 --> 20:06.371
Since he's afraid of that ability,
there's only one point he'd strike.

20:14.463 --> 20:16.215
Drop dead!

20:17.382 --> 20:19.134
The smoke won't come out?

20:20.427 --> 20:24.640
Maybe now you understand how it feels
to be someone who can't use Magic.

20:27.017 --> 20:28.518
- Shin.
- Bastard...

20:28.602 --> 20:30.604
You can't fight with those wounds.

20:31.855 --> 20:36.610
Surprised? We practice
how to defeat Sorcerers every day.

20:36.693 --> 20:38.403
You practice?

20:38.487 --> 20:43.075
Shin, it's most likely that they
stabbed you in the Sorcerer's weak point.

20:43.158 --> 20:45.494
Weak point? First I ever heard of it!

20:45.577 --> 20:49.998
Sorcerers have a special organ
to produce smoke.

20:50.082 --> 20:54.127
You've just been stabbed there
and can't produce any smoke.

20:54.211 --> 20:56.004
I see.

20:56.088 --> 20:59.007
That must be how Noi got beaten so easily.

20:59.508 --> 21:02.886
Lately, she hasn't even bothered
dodging attacks.

21:05.138 --> 21:08.475
It's been a while
since things got this fun.

21:10.352 --> 21:13.522
So you think it's fun
that you're about to be killed?

21:13.605 --> 21:17.150
Yeah. Somehow reminds me of my childhood!

21:35.085 --> 21:39.589
There isn't anything else
you or your hammer can do!

21:39.673 --> 21:42.092
Die!

21:55.314 --> 21:58.233
Looks like I had another trick
up my sleeve.

22:01.820 --> 22:04.114
You're not getting away.

22:15.751 --> 22:19.546
Just one more hit.
There's no need to hold back!

22:19.629 --> 22:20.714
Stop--

22:28.263 --> 22:30.182
This is amazing.

22:30.265 --> 22:33.560
He went through quite an unusual surgery.

22:34.144 --> 22:37.814
I think it's an operation
to enable the use of Magic.

22:38.982 --> 22:40.484
Time to get going.

22:41.068 --> 22:42.819
I have to save Noi.

22:42.903 --> 22:45.197
Wait, Noi also got captured by them?

22:45.280 --> 22:50.035
But Shin, it's honestly incredible
you're still alive with all those wounds.

22:50.118 --> 22:52.496
That's because I train on a daily basis.

22:52.579 --> 22:56.708
More importantly, you also have
a big glass shard stabbed in your head.

22:56.792 --> 22:58.585
- What?
- Look.

23:16.812 --> 23:19.606
What are you doing out here in the rain?

23:20.107 --> 23:21.608
Are you hurt somewhere?

23:24.194 --> 23:25.654
What's your name?

23:25.737 --> 23:28.657
Don't worry, I'm a doctor.

23:28.740 --> 23:30.117
A new one, though.

23:33.120 --> 23:35.330
My name is Kasukabe.

23:35.831 --> 23:39.126
Everyone calls me Haru.

23:39.209 --> 23:40.627
Nice to meet you, Haru.

23:41.128 --> 23:42.337
My name is--

23:42.421 --> 23:44.131
Mr. Kasukabe! Hey!

23:44.214 --> 23:45.382
Mr. Kasukabe!

23:49.136 --> 23:51.763
- Are you okay?
- Yeah.

23:56.518 --> 24:01.731
Haru, are you really dead now?

24:03.692 --> 24:05.402
- Shin.
- Yeah?

24:07.237 --> 24:09.614
Could you take me with you?

24:09.698 --> 24:12.826
Sure, if you want.

24:12.909 --> 24:15.328
As long as you don't slow me down.

24:15.412 --> 24:17.414
My partner's in pretty bad shape.

24:18.081 --> 24:19.458
I know.

24:20.459 --> 24:25.255
In any case,
I can see you treasure Noi a lot.

24:25.881 --> 24:28.300
Seems like you've done some growing up.

24:28.383 --> 24:29.384
Shut up.

26:01.685 --> 26:02.894
THE END

26:02.978 --> 26:05.188
What we learned in Season 2, Episode 1.

26:05.272 --> 26:07.566
Guys from the Cross-Eyes are quite frugal.

26:07.649 --> 26:09.276
Guys from the Hole are smokers.

26:09.359 --> 26:11.278
Shin and Noi don't need women.

26:11.361 --> 26:15.615
What we'll learn in Season 2, Episode 2
is still hidden in chaos.

26:15.699 --> 26:17.909
This is Dorohedoro.
